comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:42:14.109Z","harness:claude-code","Fifth projection axis censused 2026-07-29, same shape as the four already recorded here. --summary is accepted by 4 of 18 read commands: graph, deps, health and contracts. It is absent from list, list-open, context, next, get, search, validate, stats, activity, aggregate, events, history, duplicates and test-all. The absence on validate is the sharpest: validate is the most verbose diagnostic in the product and AGENTS.md routes an unsure agent to it, yet the one flag that would bound it exits 2 with Unknown option --summary. So the axis coverage table is now --fields 4 of 11, --format 6 of 11, --stream 2 of 11, ndjson 4 of 11, --summary 4 of 18, and the four commands that accept --summary are not the same four that accept --fields. An agent cannot learn one bounding idiom and apply it; it must memorize a per-command matrix. That is the row contract this item owns, and the --summary column belongs in it."
  "2026-07-29T04:48:50.084Z","harness:claude-code","Projection-declaration column measured 2026-07-29, the read-side complement of the --fields column this item already tracks. Five read surfaces declare their projection five different ways. pm list emits a projection object naming mode and the exact field list. pm context emits sections_included and names them honestly - empty at brief, six at standard, ten at deep. pm activity emits only the boolean compact with no field list. pm search emits no projection key at all. pm get emits nothing: at brief depth the envelope outside .item is completely empty and children, claim_state and linked are dropped silently, all three being present at standard. So the same question - what did this shape leave out - has one good answer, one partial answer, one boolean, one absence, and one silent drop. The good answers already exist inside the product, which makes this a generalization job rather than a design job. Note the polarity too: every declaration names what is present, never what is absent, so a caller cannot compute the complement without already knowing the full field set. Omission polarity belongs to the budget contract on pm-5t33or; which key names the projection, and that every read surface has one, belongs here."
  "2026-07-30T10:27:24.125Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: shared row_contract declares active top-level row keys, a universal jq selector, and supported/unsupported field projection across core reads and graph subcommands."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:14.598Z","harness:codex","Delivery boundary: the universal row_contract and one jq selector now cover core reads and graph subcommands, with explicit fields supported/unsupported declarations. The canonical issue remains open because inheritable --fields projection on every row surface is broader than this tranche."
  "2026-07-30T11:30:55.644Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  "2026-07-30T11:54:23.140Z","harness:codex","Review correction: graph row contracts now attach only for registered graph subcommands and include only active canonical array keys, preserving extension output ownership."
  "2026-07-30T13:06:12.870Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence for PR #829: TDD reproduced malformed declared row contracts surviving omission projection. A public structural isReadRowContract guard now validates command, unique nonempty row keys, field enums, and jq selectors; malformed built-in contracts are replaced by canonical inference and malformed noncanonical declarations are stripped. Focused projection tests and the full 6,578-test exact-coverage suite pass; SDK surface and runtime contract snapshots are current."
  "2026-07-30T13:58:35.701Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit contract clarification: declined the suggestion to reject row_keys=[] because the documented universal contract intentionally uses an empty array for commands with no top-level row collection. Added a standalone positive regression with a valid command and empty row_keys so this supported scalar/no-row shape cannot be mistaken for malformed metadata. Full 6,579-test exact coverage remains green."
  "2026-07-30T17:13:53.559Z","harness:claude-code","Row-contract coverage re-measured 2026-07-30 (evening) at HEAD, after the universal read contract shipped. The contract is real and broadly present. Of nineteen read surfaces checked, eleven now emit row_contract with a command name, a row_keys list and one jq selector: list, list-open, list-all, search, next (four row keys), context (two), get (empty row_keys for a scalar result), stats (empty), activity (compact_activity), history (compact_history), health (checks) and aggregate (groups). The declared-empty case for scalar results is documented behaviour rather than a gap.\n\nThe residual is a family rather than a scatter, and it is the family an agent cannot avoid. comments, notes and files emit no row_contract at all: their envelopes are exactly id plus count plus the collection. validate and contracts emit none either. The reason this matters more than five missing keys: pm get omits comments and notes from its payload entirely, so those three commands are the only way to read annotations, and annotation operations are the single largest family in the mutation record. The commands an agent is forced to use to reconstruct context are the ones with no declared row identity, so a consumer that discovers rows through the contract finds every collection in the product except the annotations.\n\npm events is a separate case and not a gap: it emits newline-delimited events, one JSON object per line, with no envelope to carry a contract. That should be stated in the contract documentation as a declared streaming surface rather than left to be discovered by a parser failing on line one.\n\nLinked the spec that proves the shipped half to this item, with its runnable command recorded, so the evidence is reachable from the tracker rather than only from the pull request."
  "2026-07-31T06:14:44.678Z","harness:claude-code","Measured at HEAD 2026-07-31 across nineteen read surfaces. Row contract usable (row_keys populated) on seven: list, search, history, activity, health, next, context. Present but vacuous (jq_selector published with row_keys empty, so it returns nothing) on four: deps, stats, aggregate, get. Absent entirely on seven: comments, notes, files, docs, graph, contracts, validate. No envelope at all on one: events, which emits bare NDJSON lines. The vacuous class is filed separately as pm-x710qm because it fails silently rather than loudly; this item retains the general contract."
  "2026-08-03T07:39:31.552Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: universal selector tests now cover comments, notes, learnings, files, docs, validate checks/warnings, and contracts summary/full collections. Runtime key-order acceptance was updated to require row_contract on annotation/resource envelopes."
  "2026-08-03T08:23:09.370Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance: a fresh workspace appended and read an annotation, then the published row_contract jq_selector extracted the comment without command-specific logic. The packed SDK consumer resolved comments to row_keys=[comments]."
  "2026-08-03T08:53:23.951Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary: this PR extends the universal row contract to comments, notes, learnings, files, docs, validate, and contracts; the same published selector extracted a real comment in fresh-workspace acceptance and the packed SDK resolved the contract. The item remains open because inheritable --fields projection on every row-producing surface is still broader than this tranche."
  "2026-08-03T09:06:53.307Z","harness:codex","PR evidence for delivered row-contract expansion: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/880. The canonical item remains open for the separately stated universal inheritable --fields residual."
  "2026-08-07T05:54:39.735Z","harness:codex","Active tranche 2026-08-07: complete the residual universal projection contract needed by pm-hid9g1. The shared egress layer must traverse declared nested row paths and apply one SDK-owned session projection consistently across CLI, MCP, and embedded runtime surfaces; no command-local projection forks."
  "2026-08-07T06:28:08.642Z","harness:codex","Implementation checkpoint 2026-08-07: the residual projection path now resolves row_contract.row_keys as dot paths and applies include, amount, session references, counting, and budget compaction consistently to nested arrays and object maps. Focused tests cover graph.nodes projection and object-map compaction; the existing universal jq selector remains the public extraction contract."
  "2026-08-07T06:53:13.779Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: universal read-row projections are included in the full pnpm test:coverage pass: 438 files, 6,898 tests, exact 100/100/100/100. Focused tests prove array and object-map row counting, mapping, bounding, nested-path rejection, mixed row compaction, and real temporary-tracker transport behavior."
  "2026-08-07T06:58:36.774Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance 2026-08-07: fresh temporary tracker list and search traversed the shared row contract without command-specific adapters; list delivered two facts, search replaced both with resolvable references, and exact whole-envelope receipts remained within budget."
  "2026-08-07T07:02:20.297Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: the canonical --output-include/--output-limit contract now supersedes the fragmented legacy --fields family across all 19 declared read surfaces. Shared dot-path rows cover nested arrays and object maps; CLI, SDK, MCP schemas, completions, and package egress consume the same declaration. Streaming remains explicitly documented. Full exact coverage, linked PM tests, contract checks, manual temporary-tracker acceptance, and quality gates pass."
  "2026-08-07T07:30:50.457Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/927 carries the completed nested array/object-map read-row projection contract and cross-call composition consumer."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:21:48.318Z","harness:claude-code","Cheap-form census extends this item's row-contract axis with a fourth flag, --summary, measured 2026-07-30. Present and effective on pm health (727 B vs 127,582 B plain, 175x), pm graph impact (488 B vs 223,214 B, 457x) and pm contracts (5,966 B vs 125,193 B). Absent entirely on pm context, which is both the orientation surface the agent guidance routes to first and a 9,067 B default payload with no cheap form at all - pm context --summary exits 2 as an unknown option. So the surface offers a bounded projection on three diagnostic commands and none on the one read that every agent session begins with.\n\nScope note: this stays inside this item's projection-and-row-identity boundary. It is not the streaming axis, not the encoding axis, not the list-family split, and not the zero-fill envelope class."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T07:02:19.515Z","harness:codex","A universal row primitive must treat row_contract.row_keys as dot paths and support both arrays and keyed object maps; otherwise graph-shaped SDK results silently bypass projection, counting, compaction, and session composition."
